<title>RUSSIA: Russian 182-day T-bill yields 28.15 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 182-day T-bill yields 28.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 182-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 28.15 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in the 28.02-28.74 percent range.</p>
<p>The 22070 bills, maturing on November 19, 1997, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 87.19, to yield 28.22 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number			     22083</p>
<p>    Volume					7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			    9.44 trln</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)				 8.24 trln</p>
<p>    Sold					  5.91 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				    5.18 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			     87.69 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		   87.61 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			     28.15 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		  28.36 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor					 182 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			     Nov 12, 1997</p>
<p>On May 14, the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles of a new 714-day tranche of the series 24012 OFZ interest-bearing bonds.</p>
<p>It will also repay about 7.18 trillion roubles in maturing 224-day T-bills (series 22052).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
